  "answer": "Based on my research of the UN Secretary-General list and CIA World Factbook data for borders and official languages, the countries meeting all criteria are:\n\n**Norway** — borders Sweden, Finland, Russia (3 countries); Norway's official languages (Bokmål Norwegian, Nynorsk Norwegian, Sami) are not shared with any neighbor.\n\n**Burma** — borders Bangladesh, China, India, Laos, Thailand (5 countries); Burma's official language (Burmese) is not shared with any neighbor.\n\n**Austria** — borders 8 countries; shares official languages with 5 (Germany, Hungary, Liechtenstein, Slovenia, Switzerland via German/Hungarian/Slovene), but does NOT share with Czech Republic, Italy, Slovakia (3 countries).\n\n**Ghana** — borders Côte d'Ivoire, Burkina Faso, Togo (3 countries); Ghana's official language (English) is not shared with any neighbor (all use French).\n\nCountry names as listed on the CIA World Factbook – Languages pages:\n- Norway\n- Burma\n- Austria\n- Ghana",
